  <div class="notice"><strong>Interface example only.</strong> This workflow has not been proposed or endorsed by the workshop. Its scientific rationale and connection to the breakout await review. It is not a commitment or a record of completed work.</div>
  <div class="content-columns"><div class="reading"><section><h2>Starting point</h2><p><a href="/questions/theory-and-modelling">Theory &amp; modeling — question awaiting review</a>. No analysis can be defined until the question, evidence and intended diagnostic are approved.</p></section><section><h2>Illustrative workflow</h2><ol class="workflow-list"><li><div><h3>Select an approved question</h3><p>A researcher chooses the reviewed question and defines what would count as evidence.</p></div></li><li><div><h3>Assemble the source context</h3><p>An agent could organize approved references and available data definitions while retaining versions and coverage limits.</p></div></li><li><div><h3>Prepare a reproducible analysis plan</h3><p>An agent could draft procedures, diagnostic comparisons and expected outputs for expert review before any analysis.</p></div></li><li><div><h3>Check interpretation with a researcher</h3><p>Results would require scientific assessment, explicit uncertainty and a check that the evidence supports the stated claim.</p></div></li></ol></section><section><h2>Expected outputs &amp; limitations</h2><p>A versioned analysis plan and evidence inventory could be possible outputs. No dataset, model, numerical result or scientific mechanism has been selected. This page does not initiate research or establish a causal inference.</p></section></div><aside><h2>Trace the context</h2><dl class="metadata"><dt>Question</dt><dd><a href="/questions/theory-and-modelling">Question placeholder</a></dd><dt>Highlight</dt><dd><a href="/videos/breakout-themes-3-4">Themes 3 + 4 · 1:00</a></dd><dt>Scientific rationale</dt><dd>Not yet reviewed</dd><dt>Nature of this page</dt><dd>Generic illustrative interface copy</dd></dl></aside></div>
</Base>
